-- #1867 (S1): A TRUNCATED OBLIGATION MUST NOT DECIDE AMBIGUITY.
--
-- Hand-derived from DICT-SEMANTICS §3 BEFORE running anything.  `useIx`'s context
-- is `(Ix a Char, Ix a Bool)`; at `useIx 5` it instantiates to the two GROUND
-- predicates `Ix Int Char` (222) and `Ix Int Bool` (111), each matching exactly
-- one impl by (inst).  Neither is ambiguous, and the program must print 333.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS PINS.  `recordCallObligations` records one obligation per SHATTERED
-- per-tyvar dict slot, so this call site ALSO records the 1-ary goal `Ix Int` --
-- the second parameter of a two-parameter predicate simply dropped.  That
-- truncation is deliberate (widening it moves emitted dict arity; the site's own
-- header records the #1161 decision), and it is harmless as long as the truncated
-- goal is not allowed to DECIDE anything.  It was: `checkOneCallObligation` at
-- arity 1 uses `implMatchesReceiverU`, which matches on the receiver ALONE, so
-- `Ix Int` matched BOTH impls; `checkNestedReqs` then posed that 1-ary goal to the
-- min⊑ selector, which found two ⊑-incomparable candidates and reported
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` on a program with no ambiguity in it.
--
-- MEASURED at `44257622` (the merge-base with main) on this tree, cold built:
-- `check` exit 0 printing `main : Unit` and `check --json` with ZERO diagnostics,
-- but `run` and `build` BOTH exit 1 with the unlocated
-- "type error ... detected during elaboration ... see issue #1812" surface -- so
-- the three verbs DISAGREED, and the one diagnostic that existed was never
-- rendered.  That verb split is why this row asserts all three columns.
--
-- 🚨 IT MUST BE A DIRECTORY FIXTURE, NOT A SINGLE FILE.  The same source as ONE
-- module prints 333 at exit 0 even at the base: the ambiguity diagnostic is
-- recorded there too, but the single-module `run` path never surfaces it.  A
-- flat `.mdk` sibling of this file would have been GREEN at the base and pinned
-- nothing.
--
-- ⚠️ THE FAIL-CAPABLE HALF is `s-nary-truncated-goal-joint-rejects/`: deferring a
-- truncated goal is only sound because the JOINT obligation decides in its place,
-- and that sibling is the row which fails if the joint obligation ever stops
-- being checked.  Neither file is meaningful alone.
import lib.{useIx}

main = println (useIx 5)
